## Update trellis

Renovate opens a pull request in its weekly run after trellis tags a new version. Before you merge
it, read that version's section in trellis's
[CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/265866/trellis/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md): its "Action required in
projects" part says what to do before or after the update merges. To update by hand:

```sh
uvx copier update --defaults
```

An update never touches `crates/`, `Cargo.lock`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/design.md` or `README.md`,
which are yours after the project is generated. A new project's README starts as an outline, and
one generated before trellis wrote outlines stays as it was.
{%- if interfaces | select('in', ['web', 'desktop', 'terminal']) | list %} An update doesn't touch
`docs/usage.md` either, the screenshots page, if the project has one.
{%- endif %}
{%- if published %}
The crate's `LICENSE*` files are the exception: they follow the license answer.
{%- endif %}

An update can change `readme_sections` in `Cargo.toml`, which lists the README's `##` sections,
while the README keeps its own: `just policy` then fails until you rename or add the README's
sections to match, in the update's pull request. The version's CHANGELOG entry says when it does.

An update is a rule change, so it can't also change code. Copier merges the new template into
your edits to the files it renders, such as a crate's row in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and its settings in
`Cargo.toml` and `release-plz.toml`. Where trellis changed a line you changed, or one next to it,
Copier leaves conflict markers; resolve them before you commit. Once the update merges, run
`just check-github` on `main`. A newer trellis can set more than the one you set up with, so if it
reports a wrong setting, run `just setup-github`.
{%- if kind == 'service' %}

An update that moves the base images' digests in the `Containerfile`, such as for a security fix,
publishes no new image by itself. The release workflow builds the image only when it tags a
release, and release-plz opens a release pull request only when a file of one of the crates
changes; the `Containerfile` is in none of them. The new base images ship with the next release.
{%- endif %}

## Renew the release token

A fine-grained token expires on the date you set when you created it. In its last 14 days, the
release workflow's **Update the release PR** job warns on every run. Before it expires, create a
new one with the same access and replace the secret:

```sh
just set-release-token
```

Until you do, the **Update the release PR** job fails at its token check, which names what the
token lacks, and the release pull request stops updating.
